.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_ONE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_one \- look up a single-valued query parameter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_req_query_one(chttpsvr_req *req,
                                      const char *key,
                                      const char **val_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Looks up a query parameter that must appear exactly once.  It matches
key against the URL-decoded keys of the query string, exactly as
chttpsvr_req_query does.  This
function tells an out-of-memory failure apart from a key that is
absent, and chttpsvr_req_query cannot do that.  It also allocates no
scratch array for the result.

On any failure return it sets *val_out to NULL, when val_out itself is
not NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success; the function found exactly one value and stored it in
*val_out.
ccol_key_not_found; the key is absent.
ccol_not_permitted; the key appears more than once.
ccol_not_enough_memory; the library could not allocate the parse
buffer for the query string.
ccol_invalid_args; req or key is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_oom (3)
